We need to add sound effects: thrust sound, collision, maybe background music. We need to load audio assets. Since we cannot fetch external files? We could use Web Audio API to generate simple tones. Simpler: create Audio objects pointing to data URLs maybe? Could use oscillator. Simpler: add basic beep using AudioContext.

Implement: create AudioContext, create buffer for thrust (short burst) and collision (crash). When thrust applied, play thrust sound. When game over, play crash sound. Maybe background music loop.

We need to edit game.js to add sound init and play functions. Also need to emit sound on events.

Let's edit: add at top after canvas init: create audio context, define functions playThrust, playCrash, maybe playBackground loop (simple oscillator). Use oscillator for thrust each time thrust applied; stop after short time.

Implementation: const audioCtx = new (window.AudioContext || window.webkitAudioContext)();

function playSound(frequency, duration) { const osc = audioCtx.createOscillator(); const gain = audioCtx.createGain(); osc.type = 'square'; osc.frequency.setValueAtTime(frequency, audioCtx.currentTime); osc.connect(gain); gain.connect(audioCtx.destination); gain.gain.setValueAtTime(0.1, audioCtx.currentTime); osc.start(); osc.stop(audioCtx.currentTime + duration); }

Thrust: playSound(300, 0.1); Crash: playSound(100, 0.5);

Add call in applyThrust and endGame.

Also may add background music: create periodic oscillator? Could skip.

Implement edits.

